course: dictionary
lesson: 6935
title: A doctor for children
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words look long and tricky, but you can work out a lot from the sentence around them. Paediatrician has the Greek idea of child inside it, and the sentence often tells you the meaning straight away.
explain: «In the USA and many other countries children often see a paediatrician, a children's doctor, for everyday care.» The words «a children's doctor» come right after the hard word, like a friendly explanation. Swap the meaning in: children often see a children's doctor for everyday care. It makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «In the UK children usually see a GP and meet paediatricians in hospital.» Here the clues are children and hospital. A paediatrician is a doctor who works with children in hospitals. In the USA the word is often spelled pediatrician, without the first a, but it means the same thing.
fact: A paediatrician is a doctor who looks after babies, children and teenagers and treats their illnesses.
fact: A paediatrician also checks that a child is growing and developing well, even when the child is not ill.
fact: In the UK, children usually see a GP (family doctor) first, and may be sent to a paediatrician in hospital.
fact: Useful phrases: «see a paediatrician», «a children's hospital paediatrician», «referred to a paediatrician».
fact: Paediatrician is a noun, and its plural is paediatricians.
exercise: «In the USA children often see a paediatrician, a children's doctor, for everyday care.» What is a paediatrician? | A teacher who works in a school | A driver who takes people to hospital | *A doctor who looks after children | A doctor who only treats grown-ups
exercise: «In the UK children usually see a GP and meet paediatricians in hospital.» Where do children meet paediatricians in this sentence? | On the bus | *In hospital | At the shops | At school
exercise: A paediatrician checks that a child is growing and developing well. Does a paediatrician only see children who are ill? | No, they only work with teenagers | *No, they also check children who are well | Yes, they only see ill children | Yes, but only at the weekend
test: Ravi's GP referred him to a paediatrician. Who will Ravi probably see next? | A dentist for teeth | A children's doctor | *A doctor for children who checks their health and growth | A vet for pets
test: Which word in «in the UK children usually see a GP» is the family doctor? | Children | *GP | See | Usually
exam: «In the USA and many other countries children often see a paediatrician, a children's doctor, for everyday care.» What does paediatrician mean? | A doctor who only treats adults | A person who sells medicine in a shop | *A doctor who looks after babies, children and teenagers | A school nurse who gives out plasters
